Package: frmtmb.survival
Title: Survival Families for 'frmtmb' Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Alex", "Forrence", email = "alex.forrence@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-9728-6337"))
Description: Two survival families for 'frmtmb'. The first is the
    proportional hazards model 'brms' calls 'cox()', with an M-spline
    baseline hazard whose weights form a simplex. The second is the
    flexible parametric family of Royston and Parmar (2002), which
    writes the log cumulative hazard as a natural cubic spline in log
    time. It is parameterized exactly as 'flexsurv::flexsurvspline'
    parameterizes it, so the two log likelihoods are the same number
    rather than two numbers that ought to agree, and covariates reach
    the spline coefficients as proportional hazards on the first and as
    time-varying effects on the rest. Right, left and interval
    censoring, truncation and random-effect frailties come from the
    'frmtmb' formula grammar.
